# P70 on GtkBackend on macOS (TEST_BACKEND=gtk4): focus moved by clicks on the fields, never by the focus buttons, must still reach @FocusState and its counter; then ask both for focus.
# Measured 2026-10-16 from p70-macos-gtk4-final-20261016-022612.png (1120x1176, halved to 560x588; origin=frame, 28 pt native title bar, geometry frame=(680,214) client=(680,242)): name field y 192-224, email y 236-268, ask both for focus y 393-427.
# The AppKit file's back to name click (280,225) landed just below the name field and ask both (85,375) on the a plain Text label on GTK's layout (gtk4-aim-20261016.csv2). The email click had landed and is re-centred.
# After this file: the focus has gone email then back to name (focus changes heard 3 counting the launch focus) and refusal check reports the disabled button refused.
# macOS 上 GtkBackend 的 P70:name 欄與 ask both for focus 依 GTK 擷圖重新量測。
sleep,,,,,,600000,let the window settle and take its own first responder,macos
click,280,252,frame,left,,,click the email field (re-centred) -- the app did not ask for this,macos
sleep,,,,,,500000,,macos
click,280,208,frame,left,,,and back to name (was 280;225 just below the field),macos
sleep,,,,,,500000,,macos
click,93,410,frame,left,,,ask both for focus (was 85;375 on the a plain Text label) -- the disabled button must be refused,macos
sleep,,,,,,700000,let the refusal be reported,macos
